Z||000000||Jeffrx7||10-08-2001||12:13 PM||||I previously posted with the same prob, thought it was fixed, but after getting stranded yesterday, i know it's not.  The problem is that the car will fire up and run for a couple seconds just fine, then shut off.  I got some advice before that it could be the oil pressure switch, so i fiddled with that, and it fired up and ran.  I drove it around all day with no problems at all.  The next day I was on my way to work, and after a perfect start, it died about a mile from my house.  No warning, just suddenly shut off and i was coasting.  It then would turn over fine, but wouldn't even pop.  I came back for it after work and it was doing the start and quit drill again, got it towed back to my house and I've been trying to go through the wiring ever since because this sound electrical or fuel related to me.  I cleaned and tightened every connection on the engine, which hasn't helped anything. half of the engine sensors have been replaced along with the fuel pump and ECM at some point.  I'm truthfully lost and dont know what to do next.  Any suggestions?  Thanks for any help you've got to give.<BR>~Jeff||||reg||1
