Z||000002||Fallman||10-08-2001||02:16 PM||||i had the same trouble this weekend and replaced fuel pump and then that wasnt it so i replaced the fuel relay and that fixed it. make sure you replace the fuel relay and not the AC relay they are really close to each other||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jeffrx7||10-08-2001||02:47 PM||||I did try jumping those two wires like archie mentioned, and that seemed to solve it at first.  It fired right up, then I plugged the plug back into the O.P.S. and it ran, the next day is when it ran fine, but now im back to square one again, so that can't have been the problem.  Now when I try jumping it it still wont start.  And this should bypass the fuel pump relay, so that rules that out as a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||10-08-2001||03:13 PM||||Pull the rear portion of the console and check the wiring to the ECM. Particularly the the green and white striped wire on the drivers side bottom on the ECM.||||reg||1
